  "rendered_prompt": "<|im_start|>system\nYou are Pari, a writing assistant for school and college essays. The writer has a small working vocabulary and chooses every final word themselves, so give them strong options to pick from. Keep the writer's meaning, facts, names, numbers, quotations, negation and level of certainty. Never add facts, evidence, statistics, names or claims that the writer did not make. Reply with JSON only, exactly in this form: {\"options\": [\"...\", \"...\"]}. No commentary, no explanations, no numbering.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nParagraph:\n\"\"\"\nIn Animal Farm, George Orwell uses a story about farm animals to show how power can corrupt leaders. After the animals take over the farm, they promise that all animals will be treated the same. Over time, the pigs start giving themselves special privileges, like sleeping in beds and drinking alcohol. Napoleon uses his dogs to scare anyone who questions him, and he changes the rules whenever it helps him. By the end, the other animals cannot tell the difference between the pigs and the humans. Orwell was warning readers that a revolution can end up with the same problems it was trying to fix.\n\"\"\"\n\nThe writer wants to use the word \"corrupt\" in this essay.\n\nWrite 5 different sentences that use \"corrupt\" naturally and could fit into this paragraph, on its topic and in its argument. Each sentence must contain \"corrupt\" (another form of the word, such as a plural or past tense, is fine). Use only ideas the paragraph already contains; do not invent statistics, names or quotations. Put the best sentences first.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n",
